# Per-strategy stops replacing the bot-wide kill switch (Sizhe 24 Oct: "shut only the strategy that caused the kill
# switch ... but make sure this doesn't do anything bad").
#
# Base: a3544a8. 22 files, +3104 / -27. Apply from the repo root (git apply skips this header):
#     git apply --index research_notes/strategy_kill_wiring.diff && bash deploy/precheck.sh
# Switch: config.json "strategy_stops_enabled": true. Rollback: set it false (today's 30-min bot-wide switch comes back
# unchanged); the zero-EV cap and its guard test stay either way.
#
# What it does
#   sigbot/strategy_stops.py: per-strategy ledgers rebuilt from fills each cycle (orders.purpose, then arb_trades ids,
#     else untagged), valued at the touch (catch-up / shock at mids, sets at payout basis). Stops since armed: hf_arb
#     -200 (churn_kill), catch-up -50, cheapfav -500, MM -300, arb+recycles -300, direction -300, shock -3,000; also a
#     400 trailing-hour drop (cheapfav its limit, shock none). A first breach HOLDs entries; confirmed 60 s later.
#     MM markout < -1 on 20+ fills -> mm only. Exits / unwinds / raises crossing zero -> the sender (confirmed after
#     180 s). Untagged loss >= 200 / unattributed >= 2,000 (3 evaluations, 300 s) -> the strategies that traded the
#     legs; unattributed with no suspect -> KILL-ENTRIES (all new entries; exits continue, stale quotes still pulled).
#     Stuck orders cancelled + owner paused. Bypass of a pause -> all. Ping-pong -> arb + hf_arb. 800/h bot-wide
#     backstop pauses each losing active strategy. Never stops the process.
#   Pauses are written to params/strategy_kill.json (the monitor's file; persist across restarts; only Sizhe clears),
#     logged as KILL-STRATEGY / KILL-ENTRIES; deploy/watch_deploy.py alerts on them without stopping the bot.
#   run.py gates every entry path on strategy_paused (aliases recycle/offload->arb, inside->mm, tilt/lag/news->
#     direction, "all"); exits are gated only by their own exit:* keys. Quarantine: MM keeps off a paused strategy's
#     legs for 30 min and its resting non-exit orders there are pulled. 3 failed stops cycles -> today's switch is back on.
#   zero_ev_exits (the latent leak): on the side it closes, capped at the venue position minus what catch-up / cheapfav /
#     shock hold on that same side (one-sided: never more than base sent, whatever the read timing); nothing on a failed
#     positions read; legs with an exit/raise in the last 90 s skipped (the live double exits on 960 / 898). Guard tests
#     in tests/test_guards.py (pass with the stops on or off; the round-8 two-sided cap fails 4 of them).
#
# Evidence (round-9 code, live config, stops on, nice 5 via deploy/simq.sh)
#   tests/test_strategy_stops.py ALL PASS (89); test_guards ALL PASS (zero-EV cap tests fail with the cap removed);
#   test_strategy_monitor ALL PASS.
#   tests/sim_kill_compare.py churn_widen --bugs: RESULT OK. Every injected bug caught: untagged order, mis-tag,
#     exit crossing zero, recycler pump, double sells, stuck order; losses after the trigger no larger than today's.
#     Attributed shock-sized swing (102 legs) paused nobody for someone else's loss; worst unattributed 0.
#   precheck's sim line: 38 scenarios, 0 violations (only stop: the intended hf_arb pause on churn_widen).
#   day: 0 violations, no pause fired.
#   tests/stops_pause_check.py: paused sleeves entered 0 times, still exited, nothing re-bought; pauses survive restart.
#   tests/stops_live_replay.py on the live DB: fires only on 22 Oct 19:07 (arb -524) and 22:08 (markout), the known bug
#     evening; three evaluations on today's live state pause nothing; seen_fill starts at the latest ingest.
#   Two independent Opus high-effort adversarial reviews of the final (round-9) code: both VERDICT: SAFE TO DEPLOY.
#     (Round 8 was split 1-1 on a failed-positions-read oversell in the zero-EV cap; fixed above.)
#
# Trade-offs / notes
#   - On a big ATTRIBUTED move today's switch stops everything for 30 min; this stops only the losers (sim: shock lost
#     1,045 of its own after the swing, within its -3,000).
#   - The 3 Nov punt executor must record purpose "punt" (and ideally set stops.quiet_until around its orders); manual
#     trades count as untagged.
#   - Follow-ups, none a regression (BACKLOG 0c, before the punt executor): zero-EV exits size on gross MM/direction
#     fills and the cap does not net set / punt / election holdings (on 3 Nov a strict MM exit could sell punt shares):
#     size on each sleeve's net position and subtract those one-sided too. record_order never backfills fills.purpose
#     (0 such fills live). The punt executor must record purpose "punt" first and set stops.quiet_until (SUSTAIN 300 s vs
#     ~271 s p99 ingest lag).
#   - Minor (reviews): hf_arb / catch-up stops count since armed, not from the sleeve's own basis (nil today: churn
#     realised 0, catch-up flat); a same-batch MM fill racing a zero-EV exit is a true crossing and would pause mm /
#     direction / exit:zero_ev (0 of 153 live exits); a tolerance-excused crossing candidate is not re-judged.
